# Everything the app writes for itself. All of it lives under HARMON3_HOME, which
# defaults to the checkout (harmon3/config.py), so a fresh clone regenerates the lot on
# first run and none of it is worth a diff.
#
# settings.json and scenes/ are the ones that matter: they carry prompt text, the upload
# cache and absolute paths to whatever source material was last loaded. They belong to
# whoever ran the app, not to the project.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, all of them: a bare "settings.json" matches at every
# level and would have quietly swallowed .claude/settings.json too.
/settings.json
/ui_state.ini
/scenes/
/runs/
/reference_bundle/

# Model weights. ViTPose-L is 1.2GB and YOLOX another 351MB, and setup.bat fetches both.
/models/

# Engineering notes: what was learned building this, the bugs and their lessons, and the
# ComfyUI internals read from source. Local only, by choice. README.md is the public one.
/DEVNOTES.md

# Environment
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Claude Code's config. settings.json here is the *project-scoped* file rather than a
# personal one, so committing it applies its rules to anyone who clones and opens Claude
# Code in this directory -- and the rule it carries pre-approves running arbitrary Python
# through the venv. That is a convenience only the author benefits from, so it stays out.
# Un-ignore a specific path if something in here ever becomes useful to a contributor.
/.claude/

# Editors and OS droppings
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
